# SafeSwap frontend — copy to .env (or .env.local) and fill in. All build-time via Vite, so they are PUBLIC; never put a
# secret here (the relayer's private key lives only in the server). The mined contract addresses are hardcoded in the SDK.

# The relayer's funded EOA (submits sponsored txns, is the signed `relayer`). Required for Gasless to be offered;
# otherwise the app falls back to self-execute.
VITE_SAFESWAP_RELAYER_ADDRESS=0x...
# The relayer endpoint; defaults to same-origin /relay. Override for a separately-hosted relayer
# (e.g. with `vite dev` on a different port: VITE_RELAY_URL=http://localhost:8080/relay).
# VITE_RELAY_URL=/relay
# Dedicated read RPC. Reads (incl. BondRoute's heavy off-chain views) bypass the injected wallet's flaky endpoint and use this
# instead, with retries + a fallback to the wallet. Defaults to the chain's public RPC; set a QuickNode/Alchemy URL for best
# reliability. VITE_RPC_URL=https://sepolia.unichain.org
